[124.395074, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\nUsage: mailman [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...\r\n\r\n  The GNU Mailman mailing list management system Copyright 1998-2018 by the\r\n  Free Software Foundation, Inc. http://www.list.org\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  --version          Show the version and exit.\r\n  --run-as-root      Running mailman commands as root is not recommended and\r\n                     mailman will refuse to run as root unless this option is\r\n                     specified.\r\n  -C, --config FILE  Configuration file to use.  If not given, the environment\r\n                     variable MAILMAN_CONFIG_FILE is consulted and used if\r\n                     set.  If neither are given, a default configuration file\r\n                     is loaded.\r\n  -h, --help         Show this message and exit.\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  addmembers     Add all member addresses in FILENAME with delivery mode...\r\n  aliases        Regenerate the aliases appropriate for your MTA.\r\n  changeaddress  Change a user's email address from old_address to...\r\n  conf           Print the Mailman configuration.\r\n  create         Create a mailing list.\r\n  delmembers     Delete members from a mailing list.\r\n  digests        Operate on digests.\r\n  findmember     Display all memberships for a user or users with address...\r\n  gatenews       Poll the NNTP server for messages to be gatewayed to...\r\n  help           Show this help message and exit.\r\n  import21       Import Mailman 2.1 list data.\r\n  info           Information about this Mailman instance.\r\n  inject         Inject a message from a file into a mailing list's queue.\r\n  lists          List all mailing lists.\r\n  members        Display a mailing list's members.\r\n  notify         Notify list owners/moderators of pending requests.\r\n  qfile          Get information out of a queue file.\r\n  remove         Remove a mailing list.\r\n  reopen         Signal the Mailman processes to re-open their log files.\r\n  restart        Stop and restart the Mailman runner subprocesses.\r\n  shell          Operate on a mailing list.\r\n  start          Start the Mailman master and runner processes.\r\n  status         Show the current running status of the Mailman system.\r\n  stop           Stop the Mailman master and runner processes.\r\n  syncmembers    Add and delete members as necessary to syncronize a...\r\n  unshunt        Unshunt messages.\r\n  version        Display Mailman's version.\r\n  withlist       Operate on a mailing list.\r\n--- create help\r\nUsage: mailman create [OPTIONS] LISTNAME\r\n\r\n  Create a mailing list.\r\n\r\n  The 'fully qualified list name', i.e. the posting address of the mailing\r\n  list is required.  It must be a valid email address and the domain must be\r\n  registered with Mailman.  List names are forced to lower case.\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  --language CODE                 Set the list's preferred language to CODE,\r\n                                  which must be a registered two letter\r\n                                  language code.\r\n  -o, --owner OWNER               Specify a list owner email address.  If the\r\n                                  address is not currently registered with\r\n                                  Mailman, the address is registered and\r\n                                  linked to a user. Mailman will send a\r\n                                  confirmation message to the address, but it\r\n                                  will also send a list creation notice to the\r\n                                  address.  More than one owner can be\r\n                                  specified.\r\n  -n, --notify / -no-notify, -N   Notify the list owner by email that their\r\n                                  mailing list has been created.\r\n  -q, --quiet                     Print less output.\r\n  -d, --domain / -D, --no-domain  Register the mailing list's domain if not\r\n                                  yet registered.  This is the default\r\n                                  behavior, but these options are provided for\r\n                                  backward compatibility.  With -D do not\r\n                                  register the mailing list's domain.\r\n  -"]
[124.396092, "o", "h, --help                      Show this message and exit.\r\n--- withlist help\r\nUsage: mailman withlist [OPTIONS] [RUN_ARGS]...\r\n\r\n  Operate on a mailing list.\r\n\r\n  For detailed help, see --details\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -i, --interactive    Leaves you at an interactive prompt after all other\r\n                       processing is complete. This is the default unless the\r\n                       --run option is given.\r\n  -r, --run TEXT       Run a script.  The argument is the module path to a\r\n                       callable.  This callable will be imported and then, if\r\n                       --listspec/-l is also given, is called with the mailing\r\n                       list as the first argument.  If additional arguments\r\n                       are given at the end of the command line, they are\r\n                       passed as subsequent positional arguments to the\r\n                       callable.  For additional help, see --details.  If no\r\n                       --listspec/-l argument is given, the script function\r\n                       being called is called with no arguments.\r\n  --details            Print detailed instructions and exit.\r\n  -l, --listspec TEXT  A specification of the mailing list to operate on.\r\n                       This may be the posting address of the list, or its\r\n                       List-ID.  The argument can also be a Python regular\r\n                       expression, in which case it is matched against both\r\n                       the posting address and List-ID of all mailing lists.\r\n                       To use a regular expression, LISTSPEC must start with a\r\n                       ^ (and the matching is done with re.match(). LISTSPEC\r\n                       cannot be a regular expression unless --run is given.\r\n  -h, --help           Show this message and exit.\r\n\r\n"]
